engine biome(1.0)
language js(typescript, jsx)

// C14 — data-fetching: `retry` must clear the collection's stored error BEFORE the
// boundary resets, or the error rethrows in a loop.
//
// Scoped to a `<LiveQuery>` element (the retry prop of ANY other component is not
// this convention's business) and to an INLINE handler, whose body is the only
// place a single-file pattern can look for the clearError call.
//
// PARTIAL (recorded deliberately): a HOISTED handler — `retry={retryTasks}` with
// the function declared elsewhere in the file — is NOT checked. Resolving the
// identifier to its declaration is a scope question, and the naive "does the file
// mention clearError" approximation flags conformant code (lab-verified: a correct
// `<LiveQuery retry={retryTasks}>` whose hoisted handler DOES call
// `tasks.utils.clearError()` was reported by the earlier unscoped pattern).
//
// The handler shape is matched by CST node kind, not by snippets: a snippet arm
// like `function $name($params) $body` does NOT match a zero-parameter handler
// (lab-verified — `retry={function retryTasks() { … }}` slipped through), while
// `JsArrowFunctionExpression()` / `JsFunctionExpression()` cover every inline form
// (arrow with or without parameters, expression or block body, named or anonymous
// function expression).
or {
  `<LiveQuery $props>$children</LiveQuery>`,
  `<LiveQuery $props />`
} where {
  $props <: contains `retry={$handler}`,
  $handler <: or {
    JsArrowFunctionExpression(),
    JsFunctionExpression()
  },
  not $handler <: contains `$collection.utils.clearError()`,
  register_diagnostic(span=$handler, message="retry must call <x>Collection.utils.clearError() before the boundary resets, or the stored error rethrows in a loop.", severity="error")
}
